description: Binding frontend engineering standard for this repository
globs: ["src/**", "deployments/**", "index.html", "vite.config.ts", "package.json"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first. It is the binding instruction for all AI agents
and points to the frontend standard in `frontend-standards/`.

Mandatory order before writing code:
1. `frontend-standards/01-GOLDEN-RULES.md`
2. `frontend-standards/RULE-MAP.md` §1 signal scan; read every triggered rule from its file
3. The file for the task from `RULE-MAP.md` §2

Stack is fixed (React 19, Vite 8, TypeScript 6 strict, React Router 7, TanStack Query 5,
Redux Toolkit 2 narrow, Tailwind 4, react-hook-form + zod, i18next, MapLibre GL 5, Vitest,
MSW, Playwright, nginx 1.30 non-root). A dependency not in
`frontend-standards/02-TECH-VERSIONS.md` is not added; ask the user.

Before finishing: `bash frontend-standards/tools/check-standards.sh .` and
`node frontend-standards/tools/check-i18n.mjs src/shared/i18n/locales` must exit 0,
then walk `frontend-standards/15-NEW-FEATURE-CHECKLIST.md` and state skipped items.

Never: secrets in `VITE_*`/`config.js`; API data baked into the build for SEO; datasets as
`maplibregl.Marker`; literal user-visible strings; empty `catch`; git commands that change
state.
